{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen","id":106123,"title":"What are the main critisisms of Demon: the Fallen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-05T01:07:29-07:00","id":106123,"title":"What are the main critisisms of Demon: the Fallen?","content":"As the tagline says, I'm interested in what the big critisisms were of Demon: the Fallen. When the game was released I had quit White Wolf for a time, so I basically missed all the arguments at the time, I just keep hearing bits about how it invalidated other gamelines and stuff. Care to enlighten me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T01:59:05-07:00","id":106149,"title":"","content":"Well, first off, it does have some annoying mechanical issues. Nothing too extreme by cWOD standards, and it deserves a bit of a pass for only having one edition so there was no chance to iron out a lot of the kinks later. Though it also deserves a bit less of a pass because it was so late in the cWOD plenty of those problems shouldn't have been hard to spot from experience two 2-3 editions of multiple other games. Demons also had a slightly annoying set of, &quot;we scoff at your supernatural powers,&quot; traits. All demons were completely immune to supernatural mind control and fear effects. All demons could pierce any supernatural illusion made by a non-demon with a basic roll that did not factor in sort of power level in the creation of the illusion; busting through a starting level mage's Forces illusion is as easy as seeing past a 4th Gen vampire's elder Discipline based illusions. Demons sensory range for detecting supernatural effects is measured in miles, and they have an unlimited (including cross dimensional) ability to hear people talking about them if one of their two special names - so not any name or alias - is used.<br /> <br /> The fluff side of it was largely that Demon basically went out of its way to try to present a unified WOD, but forced all the other game lines into Demon's point of view in the process. It didn't necessarily invalidate other game lines, but it did frequently make it look like the fluff of the other game lines was just false history of what the Demon books really said happened. There were multiple game-lines that Demon basically said demons were responsible for directly. Demon also chose to be explicitly Abrahamic. While Vampire's main fluff is clearly Abrahamic in nature, there's plenty of reason to doubt that whatever happened actually hewed so closely to those stories. For example Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom presents a completely different take on the origin of vampires that works just as well to explain how they came to be and work the way they do. Demon said, &quot;yeah, we're fallen angels from the Bible.&quot; No attempt to make the demons in the game more of a cross-cultural phenomenon. No attempt to at least call into question whether the default Biblical take was really what happened or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T10:45:08-07:00","id":106382,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mechanically, the game is a bit of a mess. As Heavy pointed, I suppose that can be forgiven considering it only had one edition. I have no issue re-working things for my groups\u2019 use, so this isn\u2019t a huge deal for me. Personally, I like the idea of Demon\u2019s having innate uber-powers. I never got to test this with other Spalts, but I think it would be interesting to play up the summoning/binding aspects of a Demon\u2019s nature. [My take, mechanically, was Demons would be very powerful, but the other Splats would have avenues to control them. This idea is still on my \u201cTo-Do-Test-Play\u201d list.]<br /> <br /> For me, the Fluff is where the game fell apart. Heavy already summed it perfectly: Demon \u201c\u2026went out of its way to try to present a unified WOD.\u201d I could almost forgive this if they offered some explanation about what is REALLY going on with (for example) Neverborn, Umbrood, Banes, Middle-Kingdom-Demony-Thing, etc., but it doesn\u2019t. The absolute certainty that the background was presentenced with felt very shoe-horned. <br /> <br /> In VtM, characters use their Generation to determine how far removed they are from the First Vampire. In the Euro-centric outlook that many of the Clans have, this First Vampire is Caine, but there is still some mythological ambiguity surrounding the \u201cDark Father.\u201d In Demon, not really the case. They ARE fallen angels. THIS IS what happened. Half-way through the fluff of Demon, I kept expecting to see a little sidebar that suggested that the returned Fallen are remembering history flavored by their hosts\u2019 knowledge and memories. Never happened. [Oddly, the same lack of ambiguity that I found so jilting in the Corebook fit perfectly with the material in <i>Devils Due</i>. It worked better in the DA setting.]<br /> <br /> Demon was so dependent on WOD metaplot, I think it should have been a post-Splat for WrtO, not an entirely new game. Demon feels like it should have been what Orpheus was. <br /> <br /> Finally, the thing I found most off-putting. I bought <i>Demon: The Fallen</i>, expecting to read <i>Demon: The Fallen</i> and instead I ended up reading Angel: The Prophecy. I can't pick up the book without imagining Christopher Walken... </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:09:50-07:00","id":106395,"title":"","content":"Came in a bit too late to the gameline and planted its big old butt print over all the other game lines. &quot;Oh, the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Empress? They're angels. And Kukla is an angel too. And...&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah. That annoyed me.<br /> <br /> Other than that though I generally liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:40:55-07:00","id":106568,"title":"","content":"DtF was (and still is) great. The main reason people didn't like it is because they felt, like Heavy Arms said, that other lines were blurred away by Demon the Fallen's Abrahamic nature. And since someone who holds dear to his/her heart Werewolf's Triat and Mage's wide variety paradigms, it can be frustrating. The only problem I have with that reasoning is the fact that it is meant to be its own gameline - not an attempt to unify and retcon everything. Should Vampire players be mad because of Werewolf's main mythology that doesn't fit with Caine's? Or vice versa? Of course not. Some elements of the metaplot and the World of Darkness' universe have been adapted (very well I must say, at least to my tastes) to fit a DtF universe. Just like most other lines do.<br /> <br /> There's something for pretty much any kind of play. From the very mundane to plain epic, depending on what a group wants to play. And even after all these years I am still amazed at how great Creation was described, the different feel and touch for each of the Houses of demons, the factions, etc.<br /> <br /> Great game. One of my favorite lines, ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T16:01:59-07:00","id":106584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=106382#post106382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Demon, not really the case. They ARE fallen angels. THIS IS what happened. Half-way through the fluff of Demon, I kept expecting to see a little sidebar that suggested that the returned Fallen are remembering history flavored by their hosts\u2019 knowledge and memories. Never happened. [Oddly, the same lack of ambiguity that I found so jilting in the Corebook fit perfectly with the material in <i>Devils Due</i>. It worked better in the DA setting.]</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a while since I've read D:tF, but I seem to recall some wiggle room with regard to history and cosmology, as there were multiple histories in existence at some point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T23:19:36-07:00","id":106749,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to get into Demon, but the mechanics difficulties and the weird wedged in supernatural dynamics is a turn off. Especially after playing InNomine which was very similar, but much more streamlines and working well with itself as a stand alone game. I think Demon could have been it's own game world like Abberant or Exalted, it did not have to be lumped into World of Darkness. When it came out my first thoughts were &quot;Great... what next? Aliens: the Extraterrestrial? How much more are they going to cram into WoD that was just a hint before in a splat already categorized as a type of spirit? Why did this really need to be made as World of Darkness?&quot; I couldn't understand that need and it seemed to tread some very thin ice in regards to religion that I also found distasteful and very Americanized. I let others enjoy it, but I'd probably have to Homebrew the heck out of it before I could enjoy it as a diverse and dynamic system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T01:49:47-07:00","id":106791,"title":"","content":"What BloodArmor said. The whole &quot;planted it's butt&quot; grief is silly. D:tF is stand-alone, just like all the other lines. I don't hear people complaining when W:tA says Vampires are Weaver/Wyrm creations or the likes. D:tF explains the supernatural from a D:tF standpoint, which is perfectly in line with previous lines.<br /> <br /> Now, for the Abrahamic-focus criticism, this is more valid. However, I'd have to point out that this was the 1st edition of D:tF. 1st ed. V:tM was pretty solidly abrahamic too, unless my memory is off. It's hard to predict whether this would stay the case, had the line existed longer.<br /> <br /> Mechanics issues are there, as to be expected, there's mechanics issues in all the games (celerity, hello ?).<br /> <br /> I agree with BloodArmor. In terms of fitting the standard WW setup with Houses etc. D:tF does a better job than most, if not all the other lines. Not to mention D:tF is in essence the anti V:tM: Instead of starting off human and spiraling inevitably down towards monster, you start as a monster who's had a second chance through gaining insight in humanity. So, yeah, it's a terrific game, you just can't try and fit it in or crossover unless you use it as your main line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T07:39:09-07:00","id":106882,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=106791#post106791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, for the Abrahamic-focus criticism, this is more valid. However, I'd have to point out that this was the 1st edition of D:tF. 1st ed. V:tM was pretty solidly abrahamic too, unless my memory is off. It's hard to predict whether this would stay the case, had the line existed longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You remember correctly. But that was something, more or less, new at the time. Up until then, there was Akasha (?) from Anne Rice, Dracula, and (maybe) a few other things. Even though Cain(e) was completely Abrahamic, it was a new direction for vampires.<br /> <br /> When I think of \u201cdemons\u201d my mind jumps to an Abrahamic-focus. That was the story everyone knows \u2013 Satan rebelled against God, was cast down, etc. When WW actually took that route, it felt like they gave up trying; like a big piece of pentagram-engraved fan service. The only thing, metatheologically, the game did was make Lucifer sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Personally, that\u2019s why I think that focus is a huge turn off for people; the game\u2019s foundation was a clich\u00e9. My two cents\u2026 </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T08:41:04-07:00","id":106918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=106882#post106882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">You remember correctly. But that was something, more or less, new at the time. Up until then, there was Akasha (?) from Anne Rice, Dracula, and (maybe) a few other things. Even though Cain(e) was completely Abrahamic, it was a new direction for vampires.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>George R.R. Martin's vampires in Fevre Dream self-identified as the descendants of Caine long before Vampire the Masquerade was a twinkling in Mark Rein DOT Hagen's eye. Grendel is also explicitly picked out as a descendant of Caine in Beowulf.<br /> <br /> Milton suffered greatly for his &quot;positive&quot; portrayal of Lucifer in Paradise Lost. &quot;He shook the pillars of Heaven&quot; could mean either that, hey, look, big rebellion and that's ALL he managed or it could mean, this guy managed to SHAKE the foundation of God's supposedly immutable firmament with his audacity. Also, seemingly had a good reason for the whole rebellion thing.<br /> <br /> Demon's foundation may be cliche, but it's one of the most awesome and pervasive cliche's in Abrahamic culture. Which is a significant part of the world. It's a stronger and richer core myth than the assembled Vampire traditions as made sexy through modernist literature or than the various werewolf myths scattered through the world. I guess it treads a fine line though. In religious based societies, it's dead on blasphemy. In secular societies it's a cliche and possibly in poor taste.<br /> <br /> I think there is an element of &quot;Fuck you!&quot; to the whole game. Coming from the angle of someone who played RPG's back when they were Satanist traps to guide my soul to Hell. Back when demons and devils in D&amp;D had to become &quot;fiends&quot;. This game would NEVER have hit the shelves. I think the designers have a bit of that going on.<br /> <br /> It recovers the same ground In Nomine did. Not sure it did so better. In fact, if pressed, it probably didn't. (You also got to play un-Fallen angels there too, that's a plus). One of it's strengths however is exactly the problem people had with it. It was part of larger universe (even if they are all superstring alternates or difficult to manage integrations). There were all the other supernaturals out there and you could bring them in. It did suffer from, &quot;We have all the answers. We know the Truth. The rest of you are silly, ill informed and got it wrong. Bless your little souls... (and can we have those now please? We're HUNGRY.&quot;. It suffered from that A LOT. I've been able to accept it to a degree and the rest I can put down to hubris. There is no splat that suffers more from that than Demon. And that's the way it should be. Also, (too many points), this game line probably knew from the start that it was doomed. The New World was coming. So there was a sense in which they were trying to wrap things up.<br /> <br /> That being said, this is the one OWOD game I have never gotten to play. For that alone, I am interested.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-28-2016, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T12:39:08-07:00","id":107024,"title":"","content":"My issue with the &quot;DtF was, like all cWOD games, supposed to be a stand alone game and was just explaining supernaturals from their perspective,&quot; line of thought is... well the books take it way beyond that.<br /> <br /> Lucifer is, for example, explicitly responsible for the Imbued. He let that power loose amongst humanity once again.<br /> <br /> That's a bit beyond &quot;this is a stand alone game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T12:52:21-07:00","id":107034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=106918#post106918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon's foundation may be cliche, but it's one of the most awesome and pervasive cliche's in Abrahamic culture. Which is a significant part of the world. It's a stronger and richer core myth than the assembled Vampire traditions as made sexy through modernist literature or than the various werewolf myths scattered through the world. I guess it treads a fine line though. In religious based societies, it's dead on blasphemy. In secular societies it's a cliche and possibly in poor taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't own or have read any of the cWOD Demon books per say, but I'm gonna call you on the &quot;stronger and richer core myth than various werewolf myths scattered through the world&quot; thing. The Werewolf or shapeshifter 'myth' has been with us since people started painting in caves (25,000 BCE, Franco-Cantabrian caves) and there is evidence of early human altars that worshiped animals dated around 75,000 BCE. It is interesting though that the idea of the werewolf actually started out as positive, but became negative with the spread of domestic animal herding.<br /> The idea of becoming a animal is very powerful to people all over the world and still is today.<br /> <br /> I happen to be sort of secular and <i><b>IT IS</b></i> tiring since the religious in America is shoving it your face 24 hours a day (And then act outraged when you don't want to see or hear about it for the umpteenth time). Because I happen to be of Chumash descent, I never get to see the creatures I know of locally in Monster Encyclopedias ever, but those of Abrahamic? Everywhere. It's like going to a book store and trying to find mythology books, but all the book store has is Classical Greek myths. I've already read the Greek Myths! I want to know something I don't know about that's just as epic!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:01:03-07:00","id":107099,"title":"","content":"I think on top of that point, the strong and rich core demon mythology that exists in the world has only a fractional representation in DtF. For all the times I've used words like &quot;Biblical&quot; and &quot;Abrahamic,&quot; the specific implementation of demons in the game is overwhelmingly Christian and modern (though not as modern as the romanticization of vampires). There is a lot more <i>Paradise Lost</i> in DtF than there is ancient demonology. Which isn't inherently bad for it as a game, but it is part of what rankles some people when it comes to the content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:16:06-07:00","id":107106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107024#post107024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucifer is, for example, explicitly responsible for the Imbued. He let that power loose amongst humanity once again.<br /> <br /> That's a bit beyond &quot;this is a stand alone game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. The lines all do it, I gave an example from W:tA before, so here's one from V:tM, just to shake things up: Werewolves are the product of an angry, spurned Lilith and the &quot;spirits of the wild&quot;. Kinda doesn't fit with the Garou creation myth now, does it ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107099#post107099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There is a lot more <i>Paradise Lost</i> in DtF than there is ancient demonology. Which isn't inherently bad for it as a game, but it is part of what rankles some people when it comes to the content.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a lot more of Anne Rice's books and &quot;Lost Boys&quot; in V:tM than there are ancient vampiric myths too, but I don't hear people complaining about that all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T17:56:37-07:00","id":107168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107034#post107034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't own or have read any of the cWOD Demon books per say, but I'm gonna call you on the &quot;stronger and richer core myth than various werewolf myths scattered through the world&quot; thing. The Werewolf or shapeshifter 'myth' has been with us since people started painting in caves (25,000 BCE, Franco-Cantabrian caves) and there is evidence of early human altars that worshiped animals dated around 75,000 BCE. It is interesting though that the idea of the werewolf actually started out as positive, but became negative with the spread of domestic animal herding.<br /> The idea of becoming a animal is very powerful to people all over the world and still is today.<br /> <br /> I happen to be sort of secular and <i><b>IT IS</b></i> tiring since the religious in America is shoving it your face 24 hours a day (And then act outraged when you don't want to see or hear about it for the umpteenth time). Because I happen to be of Chumash descent, I never get to see the creatures I know of locally in Monster Encyclopedias ever, but those of Abrahamic? Everywhere. It's like going to a book store and trying to find mythology books, but all the book store has is Classical Greek myths. I've already read the Greek Myths! I want to know something I don't know about that's just as epic!</div> </div> </div> </div>Go to the the Scion page and ask about sources on alternate mythologies. Be prepared to be deluged. Deluged.<br /> <br /> I don't see why there being other myths means there shouldn't be a game about Judeo-Christian mythology (yup, I said that, mythology). That's what Demon is. If that's not your thing, then, cool. The issue of using Abrahamic mythology comes up on the Scion board regularly and much blood is spilled. I come down against the attempt to integrate it on the level of that game. I think it misses the point there. I suggest drawing on Canaanite mythology to get some of the same feel while keeping with the schema of the game.<br /> <br /> But Demon, that's what it's all about. Explicitly. If you want to cover demons as envisioned in other ways, Vampire, Mage, Wraith, Werewolf, Changeling, the eastern books all have great candidates. You can even envision as as broken machine-angels. But this game was supposed to be about the Abrahamic conception. Like the movie Prophecy. Like the game In Nomine.<br /> <br /> Be careful with the factoids on the werewolf thing. I can't track most of that down in the sources I have to hand from a couple of decades as a professional archaeologist. A lot of bad archaeology and downright fake stuff out there. The best &quot;earliest&quot; wolf-man I can find is from Northern Turkey about 8000 BCE. There's something from Australia from 25,000 BCE, but it's pretty equivocal. The rest. Can't find it. Not in anything I've got on Magdalenean or Aurginacian cave art (or the Gravettien or Solutrian scratch and grooves that predated it). There isn't anything that has been widely accepted as being definitive art and not something that just could be a tool or a mistake from before the Late Paleolithic (which doesn't start until well after 75,000 BC).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 06-28-2016, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T21:46:30-07:00","id":107252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107106#post107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not. The lines all do it, I gave an example from W:tA before, so here's one from V:tM, just to shake things up: Werewolves are the product of an angry, spurned Lilith and the &quot;spirits of the wild&quot;. Kinda doesn't fit with the Garou creation myth now, does it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is with your example, these are differences in the in-game mythologies of different groups. Things like the truth behind the Imbued are stated as canonical facts in OOC sections, not just presentations of mythology and unreliable narrator sections.<br /> <br /> What DtF does would be more like VtM fully detailing Lilith, directly stating that despite whatever WtA says she is directly responsible for the shapeshifters of the world, and then later a WtA book retcons that all Garou mythology is a lie and VtM is right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's a lot more of Anne Rice's books and &quot;Lost Boys&quot; in V:tM than there are ancient vampiric myths too, but I don't hear people complaining about that all the time. </div> </div> </div>I can put forward plenty of reasons for why there is a difference, but ultimately it doesn't matter. VtM's choices didn't rankle people as much as DtF's choices did. It isn't about DtF being a bad game for what it is supposed to be, but that what it is supposed to be didn't hit the target audience as well as it could have. I would say that Wraith had a similar issue in that the quality of the game itself was never the problem, but the premise itself was a hard sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T16:56:39-07:00","id":107781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107106#post107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's not. The lines all do it, I gave an example from W:tA before, so here's one from V:tM, just to shake things up: Werewolves are the product of an angry, spurned Lilith and the &quot;spirits of the wild&quot;. Kinda doesn't fit with the Garou creation myth now, does it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was thier perspective. Their reasoning for it because that makes the most sense to vampires instead of bothering to talk with one of the beasts and find out more. You need to get Werewolf Lore of at least 3 before Werewolves are more than just angry spawn of Lillith. Same goes for Werewolves and calling Vampires Wyrm Spawn instead of Cain Spawn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107106#post107106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there's a lot more of Anne Rice's books and &quot;Lost Boys&quot; in V:tM than there are ancient vampiric myths too, but I don't hear people complaining about that all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You wanna hear complaints about Vampire, just start a new thread. There's complaints and complainers alright. Loads of them. Do they wanna bother complaining publicly? No because they know that the majority of Forum posters have probably played Vampire and Vampire is the reason there was a White-Wolf company in the first place. Without vampire having kicked things off successfully, there would be no Werewolf games, no Wraith Games, No Mage Games Etc. But Demon is the youngest bastard of the family and last to the party. More people can stand to do without them and never notice they were gone. Demons of any Homebrew can be added to games like Wraith, or as Paradox Spirits in Mage or as vile strange entities in a Werewolf's Umbra.<br /> <br /> The only system I find more unnessesary than Demon is Mummy. But that's an opinion for another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T17:05:31-07:00","id":107786,"title":"","content":"I reaaally reaaaally wish Demon took into account traits past 5, because Demons like Earthbound all start looking alike in the higher powers, and Player characters have no presented avenue for getting stronger with age like Methuselahs and the like.<br /> <br /> The Faith Pool needs to be rethought out. The stories emphasis on faith=power and with enough faith you can rebuild the world is dulled by the fact that everyone can only store a handful of faith. It wasn't even addressed what happens when your faith pool overflows, because honestly experienced demons could easily accumulate dozens of faith accruing pacts if they really wanted to.<br /> <br /> And I really wish they didn't completely remove the Umbra. I mean for the Werewolf section instead of saying they go to the Underworld when they step sideways they could have just said they enter a spirit world, or just say they vanish somewhere.<br /> <br /> It also feels like Rituals should be part of the Angel's repertoire since all the world building powers, and powers meant to make up for a lack of Lore past 5 go there, but instead its was made after the Fall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:03:33-07:00","id":107818,"title":"","content":"For me, soak is abysmally low on demons. Likewise, the pact rules, and almost all pact rules since, have been unclear whether the supernatural is supposed to fulfill their side of the contract, or if the power of the contract itself fulfills it. The answer seems to lie in a disgustingly wide pool of maybe.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with demons being Abrahamic fallen angels. To me, that's part of what makes them demons. Slapping a bunch of crap on them to make them more secular robs them of a lot of impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:08:25-07:00","id":107821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107818#post107818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, soak is abysmally low on demons. Likewise, the pact rules, and almost all pact rules since, have been unclear whether the supernatural is supposed to fulfill their side of the contract, or if the power of the contract itself fulfills it. The answer seems to lie in a disgustingly wide pool of maybe.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with demons being Abrahamic fallen angels. To me, that's part of what makes them demons. Slapping a bunch of crap on them to make them more secular robs them of a lot of impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though they did a lot of that, a lot of Demons used names from all over Mythology, like that Slayer Ravana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:09:07-07:00","id":107823,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel that DtF, along with KotE, tends to get hate just for the sake of getting hate. Yes, it has mechanical issues but then what line hasn't? But beyond that I have found both lines to have some very interesting ideas and actually quite good in their own way.<br /> <br /> In fact one of the things that have annoyed me the most at the table is when people trash those two lines without having <i>read</i> the Rulebooks. I'm not referring to anyone on the forums here it's just that in my offline experiences I've had several encounters with people who those game lines based solely on small bits they've heard elsewhere. One time I got into a debate with a guy about the backstory of DtF and it's Abrahamic origins and how he hated it. Yet at the same time he loves the idea of Caine and the Antes and if asked he will always hold Caine as the source of all vampires. So I asked him why he loved one Abrahamic origin but not the other. He had no answer beyond the vague 'DtF invalidates half the other lines' to which I pointed out that most of the lines' origin stories conflicted or invalidated other CWoD. He pointed out that the Fallen actually knew their origins as they had lived it, to which I replied that while that is true it's also worth noting that they had spent who knows how many eons in the Abyss which drove every one of them into becoming monsters and that we shouldn't necessarily consider their tales as a hundred percent true. Then I pointed out to him that the DtF actually points out that there are multiple similar but different worlds running parallel to each other, something previously brought up in MtAs, and how things can vary quite wildly from each other. For instance the first chapter the Fallen telling the story of their origins points out that in one world humanity evolved from apes, another they were created. In fact the first time I read that I felt that was WW saying 'Yeah, we've made a lot of lines with conflicting origins but that doesn't mean one's right and one's wrong, all of them are right in their world'. And surprise surprise he didn't know any of that cause he hadn't actually any of DtF's material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T20:13:11-07:00","id":107920,"title":"","content":"How about if we read the core and shook our heads at the &quot;autistic people don't have souls&quot; thing? Neurology is magic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T03:58:35-07:00","id":108079,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't have a problem who read the Rulebook and don't like the line, I just don't like people that haven't but feel that they're in the right for trashing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:57:25-07:00","id":108347,"title":"","content":"I completely feel the &quot;Didn't read it but trashes it anyway thing.&quot; I think everyone has run into that somewhere along the way.<br /> <br /> However... it also feels a bit disingenuous to me on this sort of thread unless someone actually comes out and says it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:48:27-07:00","id":108396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107920#post107920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about if we read the core and shook our heads at the &quot;autistic people don't have souls&quot; thing? Neurology is magic!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for mentioning that since I haven't read the core book. So you are saying that after the Changeling: the Dreaming's core book major <i>faux</i> pas: That said people like me needed to be killed due that having any traits of &quot;Autism&quot; as a changeling was a sign of bedlam and that I might spread it to others... (<i>Which was then repeated in the 2nd edition corebook without anyone raising eyebrows over that.</i>)<br /> Then Demon, which was written <b><i>after</i></b> Changeling of all things, then says I have no soul on top of that.<br /> <br /> I sure hope that none of the NWOD books have anything like that or anything like &quot;Indigo children&quot;. Then again, maybe at least one of them does...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Didn't read it, but trashes it anyway&quot;</i>:<br /> Did you know how expensive Demon books are on Amazon.com? One of the problems with the Revised books and near the end of 2nd. edition books is that some of them came out near the end as the whole line of CWOD was dropped for the NWOD. So there wasn't a lot of copies of those books. Meanwhile, many 1st. ed. books and early 2nd. books were often reprinted by White Wolf, so they are very easy to find and cheap. While it's true that it is cheaper to get the books via POD, I have encountered people that want the original physical copies of the books and shun any POD versions.<br /> Plus, I still haven't gotten a third or half of the Mage books, not to mention that Vampire has over 100 books. So I have a lot of reading to do before I even touch Demon.<br /> I didn't say I would not get the books in my post.<br /> <br /> Also I was explaining why someone of a secular viewpoint may not be as interested in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 04-08-2014, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:42:46-07:00","id":108462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=108396#post108396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Didn't read it, but trashes it anyway&quot;</i>:<br /> Did you know how expensive Demon books are on Amazon.com? One of the problems with the Revised books and near the end of 2nd. edition books is that some of them came out near the end as the whole line of CWOD was dropped for the NWOD. So there wasn't a lot of copies of those books. Meanwhile, many 1st. ed. books and early 2nd. books were often reprinted by White Wolf, so they are very easy to find and cheap. While it's true that it is cheaper to get the books via POD, I have encountered people that want the original physical copies of the books and shun any POD versions.<br /> Plus, I still haven't gotten a third or half of the Mage books, not to mention that Vampire has over 100 books. So I have a lot of reading to do before I even touch Demon.<br /> I didn't say I would not get the books in my post.<br /> <br /> Also I was explaining why someone of a secular viewpoint may not be as interested in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider myself quite thoroughly secular, and I have absolutely zero problem with it. The Abrahamic myth is just one myth, that's all. If I'm make-believing mythical stuff, there's nothing outrageous about assuming one myth to be &quot;true&quot; (not that Demon is true to Abrahamic faiths, what with the heavy influence from Paradise Lost).<br /> <br /> Secondly, if you can't afford or never bought the books, then you're quite perfectly allowed to not express an opinion on them. In fact, doing so despite having familiarized yourself with the material is...bordering on ignorance. Not willfull perhaps, but still. I would advise you to either read the material so you can form an informed opinon, or else simply not commenting on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T05:35:49-07:00","id":109208,"title":"","content":"I will say that overall I loved Demon. It is one of my favorite games and to date one of only a tiny handful of gaming books I have actually had the patience to read cover to cover. I literally could not put this book down. <br /> <br /> That said, it does certainly have its issues which would greatly have benefitted from a 2nd Edition. I think that they are incredibly squishy overall. I've run them in a crossover capacity both as NPCs and in a cross-sphere game and they just cannot take a hit from just about any other sphere. They have no real defensive capabilities at all and desperately need something. <br /> <br /> Also, the power scale of the Lores is a bit wonky. In several cases (notably Lore of the Forge and Lore of Paths but a few others as well) the most powerful abilities appear to be the first ones with no real need to ever get more. I think that a few of the Lores need some serious rebalancing (Seriously Lore of Flames? A first level ability that can endlessly scale damage for no cost and stacks with itself?). <br /> <br /> I would have really liked to see 6+ abilities somewhere on the scale (maybe as an Earthbound thing only if necessary) but they should be somewhere. <br /> <br /> In conclusion, I will add this for all those who haven't actually read the book. Stop bitching if you haven't read it. I stopped counting the number of complaints on this thread that are just plain provably wrong from people who hadn't read it when I got to 20, and that was still on the first page. If you don't want to play the game, fine, don't play it. But there is no need to shit all over something you know nothing about. I care very little for Werewolf, but I don't go around the Werewolf boards shitting all over it because I know I don't know much about it, and have no leg to stand on. This thread asked for specific issues with the game and its setting. Please restrict future posts to that, and only from those who've actually read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T06:07:22-07:00","id":109221,"title":"","content":"Shall there be new Forum rules that anyone who has a criticism as asked for by the poster of the thread cite page and paragraph to prove they have read the material in dispute? Maybe a minimum of three references from the first middle and end to ensure the entire book was read. [/heavy sarcasm] Look, if you ask for opinions, that's what you'll get. Whether uneducated, read from other reviews or watched someone play a completely twinkified character thumping their core book rules in everyone's face, to the devout ST with all the books memorized cover to cover and a phd in demonology besides... The fact of the matter is no one's gonna be 100% happy with Demon except for those who are willing to overlook all the inconsistencies and questionable themes. It's like discovering that Garage band with the quirky singer that screams a lot because he's still getting the hang of it. Everyone else just hates the noise. But you know they got some talent and given the chance could make great music and really go places and by God you'll be a fan no matter what. So all you Demon lovers, good for you. You obviously see something in the game that many don't because they didn't read it or read it and didn't get it. Lets leave off there because having read it or not, the criticism is not going to change anyone's mind one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T07:55:43-07:00","id":109293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=109208#post109208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I care very little for Werewolf, but I don't go around the Werewolf boards shitting all over it because I know I don't know much about it, and have no leg to stand on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a thread about criticisms of the game. If you love DtF and you see something said that you can demonstrate is explicitly untrue, go for it. But recognize that the question posed was about Demon's problems, and people coming in to voice what they felt were problems are not &quot;going around the Werewolf boards shitting all over it,&quot; they're trying to address the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This thread asked for specific issues with the game and its setting. Please restrict future posts to that, and only from those who've actually read it. </div> </div> </div>1) That's not really your call to make. You don't get to say who's read enough of the books to have an informed opinion and who hasn't.<br /> <br /> 2) You're missing a huge part of the criticism of DtF. A lot of people were disappointed in the heavily Milton-inspired presentation and core concept, so they never bothered with the rest of it. The central concepts of the game failing to snag people's interest is a valid criticism of the game and doesn't require one to have read the books to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T09:55:08-07:00","id":109381,"title":"","content":"<b>Full disclosure:</b> I <i>love </i>DTF. It hits all the right notes for me, and it stands second to Vampire for my favourite CWoD game. So, in regards to setting, the Miltonian stuff is perfect for my sensibilities. I can't comment on the merits of Demon's setting because such a discussion is ultimately too subjective to be fruitful.<br /> <br /> That said, I get why people don't like how the Demon metaplot raises more questions than answers. I think <i>the </i>Metaplot is worth a bucket of...uh, Vice Presidents...as far as mattering to <i>me</i>, but that doesn't mean I don't empathise with people who <i>are </i>invested in it, and who (perhaps rightly) thought Demon didn't fit.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm closer to the opinion that all the lines are mutually contradictory, even when crossover is <i>explicit and intended </i>(ask me about the death of the author sometime). Demon's sin was being upfront about that contradiction. But? There's a great deal of material in these games that rewards using crossover plothooks, and if one doesn't like what Demon brings to that table, that's legit.<br /> <br /> This is the problem with having game lines existing in the same world yet offering multiple creation stories. Sometimes these discussions just end up being like talking about religion.<br /> <br /> tldr: Metaplot is tricky!...?<br /> <br /> Now, as for what I don't like about Demon? Mechanically, it's kind of a mess. Of the two Demon chronicles I've been in--one of which I played, and one of which I ran, and in two completely different groups--we never, ever got the hang of the rules. We didn't even try. Mostly this came from over-complication. Many of the rules in Demon needed to be simplified. For example, Torment Invocations. The system given for accidentally invoking them is downright bizarre. It got errata'd in the Player's Guide, but it was still weird, and very un-White Wolfy.<br /> <br /> Another core feature of Demon that needed revision was True Names. The Fallen have to be vigilant in guarding their True Names, lest their enemies use those Names to control or harm them. This is (I think) intended to be <i>the </i>major limitation on Demon characters, other than the Tornent morality stat. The game gives you a really vague system for how to deal with True Names, and, in short, that system isn't suitable for an in-depth exploration of that aspect.<br /> <br /> My biggest gripe with Demon is actually less to do with mechanics, though, and more to do with the way the core was written out. The setting chapters, which are the first four chapters of the book, are written entirely in-character. That's a neat conceit...but I found it grated when what I wanted was a bit of outside perspective. It actually all reads pretty well, but it made the game a bit less accessible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-09-2014, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T10:23:41-07:00","id":109403,"title":"","content":"I don't like how we don't really have any framework to represent say Lucifer. He is too much like how they Handled Charon in Wraith, he is in theory using the same traits as everyone Else but he has undefined special powers only he and others near his level have, rather then giving us any explanation of powers beyond Rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T10:54:30-07:00","id":109443,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the Milton-inspired outlook on Demon but there were some things I disliked both in the Fluff and in the Mechanics.<br /> <br /> Fluff, I absolutely hated that DtF tried to steal the big guys of other lines for themselves, like both Charon and Nhudri. I also think a mistake was made in ignoring the Umbra altogether. Also since they went the Milton/Abrahamic route they could still have kept it a bit more open ended and mysterious, as in God could easily have been presented in a way that makes It to be a being composed of Stasis, Entropy and Dynamism aka Weaver, Wyrm and Wyld balanced, naturally in a away that it can be interpreted either way. Also I hated the fact that they basically lost almost all memories of themselves under a flood of human memories when possessing unless they had heavily invested in Legacy background. They are the creators of all things, even if the Faith to empower their work did came from a God, and should not be so easily suppressed.<br /> <br /> Also while I did like the Abrahamic take it did make it undesirable for some, even players who happily played In Nomine on both sides, so obviously it did something wrong even if I can't really put my finger on what.<br /> <br /> Also rather importantly the Fluff describes them as rather powerful beings, nearly on par with Quantum 6 or 7 Aberrants at the highest and even in the lowest at least on par with basic PC of that awesome game, able to create mountains, to destroy species or actually be the Sun etc. Unfortunately the Mechanics are totally unable to come anywhere near what the promises that the fluff makes. Yes, I get it. They are without their unlimited Faith supply and fresh out of imprisonment but still the Lore's ranged from kinda nearing awesome to being kinda sad.<br /> <br /> Which leads us to mechanics.<br /> <br /> Lore's were like said on many parts rather disappointing and on others quite nice indeed on a normal WoD scale that is but they still lacked the feeling of playing as one of the creators of our world. They really did not evoke that kind of might to me. They tried to bring that kind of might back on the table in the Earthbound book with the Mastery Background but that was only usable by the Earthbound and while it did make it possible for the m to level cities with one evocation it still only acted to boost the existing Lore's not to expand them or make them more evocative of the fluffs promises. So while it did what it was meant to do with the Earthbound, made them extremely powerful and dangerous, it did nothing to help your average Fallen to feel more angelic or demonic.<br /> Also the aforementioned Legacy background was a horrid invention. Basically required to take unless you wished to play a Fallen who did not know that it was anything other than a Human with fancy magical powers. It was mentioned earlier in this thread but Demon also forgot to handle 6+ stats and High Faith in general with excess incoming Faith apparently just lost. An enterprising Demon can easily get a rather nice income of Faith but there really was little point in doing so since most of the time it was all just wasted, which kinda screwed over whole of the Faustian agenda of gathering pacts and so being able to channel huge amounts of Faith. And as a final Mechanical problem, they were kinda squishy like someone else already mentioned, but at least they could be summoned back or could just switch Host.<br /> <br /> Switching Hosts was also something left a bit open ended by the way. Your starting character has his abilities and attributes coming mainly from the human being possessed so what happens to your non Lore, non Faith stats when you switch host? Logically fluff would suggest you learning the abilities and gaining the attributes of the new host which basically means almost completely different character, especially if your low on Legacy in which case you now remember always having been the new host with bits and pieces of previous existence. Still it was a matter kinda glossed over even though it was an important part of the game. All of this even more true if you didn't find a suitable host and fell back into the Abyss and were re-summoned.<br /> <br /> All in all while I liked DtF and wanted to like it even more, and still use some parts of it in NPC's and other things, I still ended up preferring Devil's Due which with a single book beat the whole DtF line. DD had potential if only it had gained a few more books. It took a bit different approach to Demons, in general Demons were a bit more Demonic in it, and tied your memory to your Torment and along with your memory much of your power. If you couldn't remember being able to do something you weren't. Of course it too had it's own problems, it's Arcana were on par with Disciplines and such powers and again did not carry real Demonic oomph but it still worked and had a nice Demonic tone to it, but at least the Arcana were meant to be customized and be modular in general so play groups could easily come up with greater powers if need be, and they were still somewhat squishy. Basically it was a whole new edition of Demon in a book that had almost half of it's word count dedicated to Infernalists and Demonologists instead of being mainly about Demons themselves so it was a truly epic achievement.<br /> <br /> The Theme difference between DtF and DD can be summed up to be that the former is about Fallen Angels and the latter about Demons. And yes even though both are technically the same thing the mood difference is huge.<br /> <br /> A second edition of DtF would be nice especially if it took into heart the lessons learned from DD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T11:01:11-07:00","id":109450,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah that might be my biggest complaint, they don't tell you the impact of Switching hosts! You just get that you loose a Faith Point for going back to the Abyss, but how is your Identity after you switch hosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:52:28-07:00","id":913173,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: DtF was the only WoD game I really liked, a brilliant games setting! So my opinion IS subjective....<br /> <br /> Points of criticism:<ul><li><i>The Judeo-Christian / Miltonean interpretation of the demons put of many people.</i> If you are bothered by it, for whatever reason, it is not your game. If you want multiple culture interpretation of demons, you won't like it either.</li> <li><i>DtF is best as a standalone game. </i>It does not play well with other WoD lines. The reasons are many, the point is it plays best if it stands alone. You can try to incorporate it with other lines, there are many threads around about the hows, but I found it not worth the trouble. Forget the &quot;unified&quot; Wod setting.</li> <li><i>DtF mechanics are not elegant.</i> The DtF tried to implement a similar currency/moral system as the other WoD lines, but it did not really succeed. Even after the Player's handbook errata, many problems remain. Like the Torrent system. Also the moral framework with the three Virtues felt forced for me. There was a disconnect between the rules and the fiction.</li> <li><i>Lore are limited. </i>I understand that the Fallen are limited in power, especially compared to their original being. But limiting Lores is anti-climatic. Only one of the seven Houses can open a lock (Lore of Portals, first power). Why? And why is it so difficult to learn them. I understand that some houses are experts on in some lores, that is ok. The limits felt very artificial.</li> <li>While the setting is a blast, some minor details are missing. Like the demon uses his hosts physical attributes, but what about the intellectual ones? Not a big deal, but still.</li> <li><i>&quot;WoD habits&quot; are bad for DtF.</i> Like the demonic courts, mirroring the vampirics ones. Well, it is quite bland and does not really fit well and is best omitted. Also the four political groupings are a bit bland, lacking detail.</li> <li>Metaplot...'nough said. Drop it out of the game, it does nothing to improve the game, nor the setting.</li> <li>Rushed supplements. The supplements are either great or meh. Most of them feel a bit rushed, with page XX in them, &quot;because of space limits we could not...&quot;, etc.</li> </ul><br /> That is all I can think of. None of them are really crippling though. Hope it helps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4084-michaelsd","name":"MichaelSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:56:40-07:00","id":913250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=107024#post107024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucifer is, for example, explicitly responsible for the Imbued. He let that power loose amongst humanity once again.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...HAVE YOU READ TIME OF JUDGEMENT?! HE CONSIDERS THEM AN ABERRATION AGAINST NATURE MADE BY &quot;SHE&quot;!<br /> <br /> Lucifer fought an Imbued, and he hates them more than anything","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:08:21-07:00","id":913271,"title":"","content":"Wow, that's a necro.<br /> <br /> You seem to be missing the point there. Lucifer didn't create them, nor does he like them. But his actions still let them loose in the world again. Lucifer hating the consequences of his actions are something of a running theme with him in DtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:32:07-07:00","id":913399,"title":"","content":"Yeah the Imbued were ultimately created by the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen/Phoenix who are the last Angels on Earth. And they only created the Imbued as a last resort to protect humanity and the world from everything that had been going on in the late 2E and Rev Ed of the oWoD.<br /> <br /> Of course this wasn't the first time they created the Imbued. Last time they were called the Wan Xian until they eventually became what we know today as the Kuei-Jin. Long story short, the Wan Xian got drunk and corrupt off their power and started becoming as bad as the things they were created to fight. As a result they were cursed for it.<br /> <br /> The implication being that the Imbued will eventually become powerful and from there corrupt as the Wan Xian became.<br /> <br /> So yeah Lucifer would likely recognize what the Imbued are and just as likely was around to witness what the Wan Xian became and probably doesn't want to see that again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:49:14-07:00","id":913413,"title":"","content":"Problems I had trying to get Demon going.<br /> 1. Interest. Still, it's Vampire or nothing. I was lucky enough to get Mage going.<br /> 2. Well, Demon. My friends had the problem of, you are evil, deal with it. Not to mention one person I had interested wanted to go on the redemption route. Which they didn't like, so I told them you can do whatever they wanted to do. Redemption, New World God, fuck all and go your own way. Finally got them convinced until she left so I don't have to worry about it anymore.<br /> 3. Your only antagonists is Demons, Earthbound, and Hunters. I can understand that there's not a whole lot on the same power level as Demons. But still, no Angels? Werewolves has Nexus Crawlers, no extradimensional terrors like the Cenobites. This is a minor issue since I'm trying to make Cenobites as an antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:56:49-07:00","id":913419,"title":"","content":"My personal head canon (yes, I do own Demon: the Fallen and the Earthbound sourcebook):<br /> <br /> 1. The Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen/Empress are not angels, despite what Days of Fire says. I feel that this contradicts almost everything said about these characters in both Kindred of the East and Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2. The Imbued were created by the Messengers, who ARE angels (I think this is mentioned in Hunter Storyteller's Handbook, but not 100% positive).<br /> <br /> 3. The Imbued are reincarnations of the Solar Exalted, not the Wan Xian, who were actually descended from the Dragon-Blooded (discussed in one of the First Edition Exalted books as well as Hunter: Fall from Grace).<br /> <br /> Again, this is just what I use in my own games. Anyone who disagrees is certainly welcome to offer constructive criticism/debate. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:59:29-07:00","id":913420,"title":"","content":"Still Mortal Minions. The Messengers don't fight Demons themselves. Pretty much like a powerful Vampire sending the underlings and ghouls because why should I get my hands dirty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:05:08-07:00","id":913710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=913419#post913419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal head canon (yes, I do own Demon: the Fallen and the Earthbound sourcebook):<br /> <br /> 1. The Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen/Empress are not angels, despite what Days of Fire says. I feel that this contradicts almost everything said about these characters in both Kindred of the East and Exalted.<br /> <br /> 2. The Imbued were created by the Messengers, who ARE angels (I think this is mentioned in Hunter Storyteller's Handbook, but not 100% positive).<br /> <br /> 3. The Imbued are reincarnations of the Solar Exalted, not the Wan Xian, who were actually descended from the Dragon-Blooded (discussed in one of the First Edition Exalted books as well as Hunter: Fall from Grace).<br /> <br /> Again, this is just what I use in my own games. Anyone who disagrees is certainly welcome to offer constructive criticism/debate. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically, there was a break made in the plan to make Exalted the past of a unified WoD. As of the first edition STC for Exalted, it made it sound more like they were both mutual elseworlds versions of each other, and that the similarities are basically just because WW makes stuff in the shapes given, using an analogy about how flowers of the same type can still be different even if they look very similar.<br /> <br /> So, there are tales of ancient heroes in H:tR, but they aren't the Solar Exalted. Just something that looks a lot like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:32:27-07:00","id":913742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=913399#post913399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the Imbued were ultimately created by the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen/Phoenix who are the last Angels on Earth. And they only created the Imbued as a last resort to protect humanity and the world from everything that had been going on in the late 2E and Rev Ed of the oWoD.<br /> <br /> Of course this wasn't the first time they created the Imbued. Last time they were called the Wan Xian until they eventually became what we know today as the Kuei-Jin. Long story short, the Wan Xian got drunk and corrupt off their power and started becoming as bad as the things they were created to fight. As a result they were cursed for it.<br /> <br /> The implication being that the Imbued will eventually become powerful and from there corrupt as the Wan Xian became.<br /> <br /> So yeah Lucifer would likely recognize what the Imbued are and just as likely was around to witness what the Wan Xian became and probably doesn't want to see that again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course the Wu Tien also exist so.. maybe people aren't all on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T17:55:50-07:00","id":913764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=913742#post913742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Of course the Wu Tien also exist so.. maybe people aren't all on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Wu T'ian are an entirely different thing, created by different beings, admittedly with the aid of servants of the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen but not necessarily their direct help.<br /> <br /> Plus given the stuff that had recently happened in the oWoD and what was coming, is really all that surprising that the pair would do as much as they could, make as many champions to stand against what is to come as they could?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:38:29-07:00","id":914942,"title":"","content":"This is how someone summed it up for me:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>DEMON: THE FALLEN</b><br /> <br /> All the politics of Vampire without having to hide from the sun.<br /> All the &quot;rip-em-apart&quot; power of Werewolf without Rage or silver weakness.<br /> All the earth-shattering power of Mage without Paradox.<br /> All the &quot;evel-for-the-LOLs&quot; of a Wraith's Shadow without losing your character.<br /> All the duality of Changeling without the Banality. </div> </div> </div>So, yeah, seemed like they were trying to fit some square pegs into round holes and sew up the differences. Not that I'm minded so much, but it definitely ruffled some feathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 06-15-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T21:57:54-07:00","id":915400,"title":"","content":"So a lot of people here are citing the &quot;Miltonic&quot; aspects of Demon: the Fallen, but really D:tF is more a Byronic misreading of Paradise Lost.<br /> <br /> The Devil isn't heroic in Paradise Lost. He isn't even anti-heroic as Byron put forth. He's the straight up villain, as anyone who's read the first chapter of the poem can attest.<br /> <br /> Milton did a fantastic job in writing the part of Lucifer. The Devil is so persuasive that we find ourselves caught up in his rhetoric, to the point that we view him as a noble rebel rather than an insolent traitor. You have to remind yourself that in the context of Milton, Lucifer is the prince of lies. He's manipulative, scheming, and you're hearing his side of the story.<br /> <br /> There were two main objections I had to D:tF: the first stems from this fundamental misreading of Milton, the conceit that the Fallen were somehow moved to rebel out of love and compassion for humanity rather than arrogance and scorn for the divine (Lucifer was motivated by the sin of Pride in Paradise Lost). It's a novel idea, and I don't mind that they put a little twist on things, but it gave Demons a degree of moral righteousness that frankly didn't mesh well with the core concept of the game (playing a tormented fallen angel - it just loses a lot of it's punch if you were cast down because God was a dick.)<br /> <br /> The second issue I had was with Hell itself. Hell was just plain boring. Hell was nothing - a void - literally a bunch of fallen angels all packed in a dark room for eons and eons all forming cliques and arguing over what happened to Lucifer. Anyone who's read Dante's Inferno knows how rich a landscape Hell can be - and they phoned it in with Hell in D:tF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T22:35:45-07:00","id":915408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=913764#post913764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the Wu T'ian are an entirely different thing, created by different beings, admittedly with the aid of servants of the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen but not necessarily their direct help.<br /> <br /> Plus given the stuff that had recently happened in the oWoD and what was coming, is really all that surprising that the pair would do as much as they could, make as many champions to stand against what is to come as they could?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wu Tien cover the same thematic ground as replacement Wu Xian and are probably a better job of being both in control, under divine gudience etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:51:02-07:00","id":915597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=915400#post915400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a lot of people here are citing the &quot;Miltonic&quot; aspects of Demon: the Fallen, but really D:tF is more a Byronic misreading of Paradise Lost.<br /> <br /> The Devil isn't heroic in Paradise Lost. He isn't even anti-heroic as Byron put forth. He's the straight up villain, as anyone who's read the first chapter of the poem can attest.<br /> <br /> Milton did a fantastic job in writing the part of Lucifer. The Devil is so persuasive that we find ourselves caught up in his rhetoric, to the point that we view him as a noble rebel rather than an insolent traitor. You have to remind yourself that in the context of Milton, Lucifer is the prince of lies. He's manipulative, scheming, and you're hearing his side of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Milton's Lucifer is one of literature's early examples of &quot;unintended fandom&quot; even in its own time, a fandom that Milton himself was none too pleased about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:35:37-07:00","id":915880,"title":"","content":"Thinking about my issues with the game vs some of its more ardent fans in the &quot;One true World of Darkness&quot; arguments:<br /> <br /> 1. No angels, god etc.<br /> 2. connected to that your &quot;primary conflict&quot; are super demons wanting to enslave you<br /> 3. Demons are all new, any connection to the thousands of years of other demon things showing up in human history is basically thrown out.<br /> 4.Earthbound vs fleshbound thing, becoming Earthbound when you &quot;die&quot; seems more moral than stealing another life... but that makes you fall to Torment.<br /> 5. Politics are too vampirey especially for &quot;new&quot; things.<br /> 6. Hell is boring, and isn't really hell, where are the sinners?<br /> 7. clearly needs a second edition for rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:44:23-07:00","id":916241,"title":"","content":"The two main things that kept sticking in my craw about Fallen were:<br /> <br /> 1) The general power creep it represented. Demon wasn't the first, but it was the punctuation mark. It looked at the things other splats could do and said &quot;That's cool I guess, but what if we could make them <i>completely irrelevant</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Its tendency to explain away any remaining mystery in the World of Darkness. Once again Demon wasn't the first, but it punctuated the game of cosmological one-ups-man-ship. It pays lip service in the very beginning to this idea of layered reality in which everything can simultaneously true, but afterward couldn't resist butting into any cosmological discussion with a smug &quot;Well <i>actually</i>...&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T17:15:23-07:00","id":916500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=916241#post916241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two main things that kept sticking in my craw about Fallen were:<br /> <br /> 1) The general power creep it represented. Demon wasn't the first, but it was the punctuation mark. It looked at the things other splats could do and said &quot;That's cool I guess, but what if we could make them <i>completely irrelevant</i>?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh you're playing a friggen demon. It should be powerful. People said the same thing about Mages until they got a bunch of books in revised making them totally respect vampires and not turn them into lawnchairs.. because vampires are serious business. M20 promptly included it as a commonly used Rote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Its tendency to explain away any remaining mystery in the World of Darkness. Once again Demon wasn't the first, but it punctuated the game of cosmological one-ups-man-ship. It pays lip service in the very beginning to this idea of layered reality in which everything can simultaneously true, but afterward couldn't resist butting into any cosmological discussion with a smug &quot;Well <i>actually</i>...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Layered reality IS part of the smug &quot;Well actually...it starts there with that. Of course every gameline has a &quot;smug&quot; truth about others. The issue is only Demon came out last so you don't have the werewolf, changeling or mage smug counter &quot;oh you're just...&quot; to them. Mind you Demons and changelings LOOK Alot alike... Demons are just alot more durable.. in a broad crossover game where mutability is a factor I'd argue they were just Kithain who have snuck into a more readily held belief system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T18:47:59-07:00","id":916540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=916500#post916500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh you're playing a friggen demon. It should be powerful. People said the same thing about Mages until they got a bunch of books in revised making them totally respect vampires and not turn them into lawnchairs.. because vampires are serious business. M20 promptly included it as a commonly used Rote.<br /> <br /> Layered reality IS part of the smug &quot;Well actually...it starts there with that. Of course every gameline has a &quot;smug&quot; truth about others. The issue is only Demon came out last so you don't have the werewolf, changeling or mage smug counter &quot;oh you're just...&quot; to them. Mind you Demons and changelings LOOK Alot alike... Demons are just alot more durable.. in a broad crossover game where mutability is a factor I'd argue they were just Kithain who have snuck into a more readily held belief system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've begun to feel strongly that Demon and Mage could be better positioned as sub-games under an envelope of Changeling. And also for Changelings to be more solid and less weird about a difference between mortal and fae seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:04:13-07:00","id":919310,"title":"","content":"So does anyone want an X20 Demon book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:24:58-07:00","id":919314,"title":"","content":"Maybe?<br /> <br /> I'd want to see the head developer address three things:<br /> <br /> 1) Is there going to be an effort to address the mechanics of the game that never got revisions due to the game only having one edition?<br /> 2a) Given how few books there were, what does an omnibus have to really offer? What will they add to the game to make it worth being a ~500 page book?<br /> 2b) Will there be any attempt to open up the game to a wider range of demonic origins?<br /> <br /> If those points can be addressed in fashions I find satisfactory, I'd be totally on board with it. If I'm just going to get DtF's core book + player's guide with a few minor rules tweaks... I'm not sure I want to shell out a ton of cash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:59:05-07:00","id":919334,"title":"","content":"If they're going to balance mechanics, flesh out the Pacts and some rules (like the flying rules), and make it a bit less like &quot;vampires with a different outlook&quot;, I'm in.<br /> <br /> The main criticism I have to Demon it's that it suffers a grave case of &quot;wanting to be like Vampire&quot;. Lores are like Disciplines/Thaumaturgy, they have &quot;courts&quot; in the cities, Anted-err-Archdukes, they have &quot;Humanity&quot;, Virtues, and the mechaincs to get Faith often feel like hunting/having a Ghoul. Being a Fallen Angel shouldn't be like that, it's a must to break the mold a little (like they did with Werewolf, or Mage, or with the 2.0 Demon) and make Demons a mechanic that fits their unique role and metaplot.<br /> <br /> Oh, and you either disregard the rule that forbids Demons to make pacts with Vampires, or stop implying that the demons that are always doing pacts with vampires are Demon demons. You can't have both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T22:53:22-07:00","id":919521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=919314#post919314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2b) Will there be any attempt to open up the game to a wider range of demonic origins?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Like how V20 let you play nonembraced Vampires who didn't have generation because they weren't from Caine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T23:37:26-07:00","id":919539,"title":"","content":"No, like how VtM in general doesn't actually hold the Noddist mythology as absolute fact, and that there are other myths for how vampires came to be besides the core one. I didn't say, &quot;Will there be any attempt to open up the game to a wider range of demons types?&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the criticisms of Demon is that the demons in it follow a very specific take on (a subset) of one religion's conceptualization of demons, which has nothing to do with the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:16:48-07:00","id":920200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=919539#post919539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, like how VtM in general doesn't actually hold the Noddist mythology as absolute fact, and that there are other myths for how vampires came to be besides the core one. I didn't say, &quot;Will there be any attempt to open up the game to a wider range of demons types?&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the criticisms of Demon is that the demons in it follow a very specific take on (a subset) of one religion's conceptualization of demons, which has nothing to do with the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> V:TM treats the general gist of Caine, God, Noddism as fairly true if the specifics aren't exactly there. Every other Mythology is treated as broadly wrong or the delusions of a particular clan. The Antedeluvians were active players as of DA, many who specifically interacted with Caine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T00:03:04-07:00","id":920223,"title":"","content":"And all those NPCs have conflicting stories.<br /> <br /> The point is, there's no reason for DtF to not provide options. Even if they come off as &quot;delusional&quot; because for at least some of us, those alternate mythologies are better for the game because they blunt the One True History that's supposed to not actually be cut and dry from becoming what most people treat it as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T00:57:50-07:00","id":920244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920223#post920223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all those NPCs have conflicting stories.<br /> <br /> The point is, there's no reason for DtF to not provide options. Even if they come off as &quot;delusional&quot; because for at least some of us, those alternate mythologies are better for the game because they blunt the One True History that's supposed to not actually be cut and dry from becoming what most people treat it as.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never got the impression that Mysterious past and world of conspiracies was meant to be a part of the Demon story. Its pretty cut and dry what is what. Now when you want to play crossover One World of Darkness, well there's your alternative mythologies. Mage, changeling and werewolf readily have those answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T01:17:30-07:00","id":920249,"title":"","content":"Demon doesn't have to be all things to all people. There is nothing wrong with saying 'this is our backstory, it is what it is.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T01:42:43-07:00","id":920256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920244#post920244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got the impression that Mysterious past and world of conspiracies was meant to be a part of the Demon story.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the mysterious past was never meant to be part of Demon... why do Demons have the Legacy Background that's specifically designed to make the past mysterious for them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920249#post920249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon doesn't have to be all things to all people. There is nothing wrong with saying 'this is our backstory, it is what it is.'</div> </div> </div> </div>At the same time, Demon doesn't have to be needlessly restrictive either. If you can make it be more things to more people with zero sacrifice to what's there, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T01:59:42-07:00","id":920257,"title":"","content":"Because there is a value to thematic and mythological consistency when it is in service to the game's overarching themes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T02:17:46-07:00","id":920260,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest beef was that it was trying to be In Nomine, just edgier. And frankly, I've got a superior version of that game already, and a million ways to use demons in all the other WoD games without bothering with Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T05:56:24-07:00","id":920308,"title":"","content":"I personally really like Demon, although I wouldn't want a D20 edition because there really isn't enough information. Demon Second Edition would be cool, especially if they made the time before demons were imprisoned less clear or got rid of the Legacy background.<br /> <br /> Now, one of my beefs with Demons is that they just aren't powerful enough to me. Several Lores are just a letdown, and Tormented versions of the powers generally seem to be useless or annoying (Lore of Humanity 1 could be a really useful power, but the Tormented version simply makes it a gamble). I'm not even sure the tormented versions should have been a thing.<br /> <br /> Now I don't own In Nomine, so it might be better, but I think that Demon manages to hit that point in the World of Darkness that Vampire never quite managed for me. Now it's not my favourite game, that would be Mage, but It's certainly up there for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T12:25:44-07:00","id":920501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920257#post920257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there is a value to thematic and mythological consistency when it is in service to the game's overarching themes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, demons not being 100% certain on how the distant past really unfolded, as well as partially losing themselves in the possession process implies that the game's overarching themes are better served with more ambiguity; not less.<br /> <br /> And, you know, it's also something a few people here at a minimum are saying would be influential to their desire for more DtF products. DtF is a small game line that needs work, but it doesn't need a giant omnibus edition. If it's going to get a D20, it needs to add to whats there; not just add in some errata. Otherwise, what's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920308#post920308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I don't own In Nomine, so it might be better, but I think that Demon manages to hit that point in the World of Darkness that Vampire never quite managed for me. Now it's not my favourite game, that would be Mage, but It's certainly up there for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Nomine is complicated. Conceptually it's a better game than DtF as a stand-alone, but it isn't setup for the WoD. Rules-wise... I have trouble thinking of In Nomine as better than DtF though... it's' kind of a mess.<br /> <br /> Part of In Nomine's problem is that it's already the &quot;darker and grittier&quot; version of a French game (In Nomine Satanis/Magna Veritas) which is supposed to be more comedic in the vein of the novel Good Omens. So it's tonally all over the place. So DtF is also a bit better at knowing what it wants to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T01:14:58-07:00","id":920874,"title":"","content":"The Central Theme of the setting is you served the Creator of the World and Fell. Why you fell? how you fell? these are points of ambiguity. Whether you are a fallen angel? that is no more a question that needs ambiguity than whether Vampire needs the possibility taht your character is just a crazy guy who drinks blood or Werewolf needs to have a counter Gaia narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T01:39:51-07:00","id":920878,"title":"","content":"So.... yeah, you don't care at all what I'm actually saying about this. Gotcha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T06:43:52-07:00","id":920937,"title":"","content":"It would be better if we would try to stay constructive in the discussion, just saying <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:58:41-07:00","id":920957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920501#post920501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, though, demons not being 100% certain on how the distant past really unfolded, as well as partially losing themselves in the possession process implies that the game's overarching themes are better served with more ambiguity; not less.<br /> <br /> And, you know, it's also something a few people here at a minimum are saying would be influential to their desire for more DtF products. DtF is a small game line that needs work, but it doesn't need a giant omnibus edition. If it's going to get a D20, it needs to add to whats there; not just add in some errata. Otherwise, what's the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it doesn't suggest that at all. You're mistaking the set dressing for the thematic core of the game, which is ultimately about the dangers inherent in choice, the value or lack of value of hope and trust, and how actions can have unintended and horrific consequences very, very far down the line. Diluting the origin of the demons involved serves no purpose, and having literally <i>all</i> that has gone wrong for them and for mankind stem from a single unprecedented act of Choice ties thematically to the central question of the gameline in a way six different origin myths can't.<br /> <br /> As for a 20th Anniversary, I don't recall arguing for one at any point. Can you show me where I have?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T10:06:25-07:00","id":921006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920957#post920957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it doesn't suggest that at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement doesn't seem supported by either the text, or your following comments. What you cite as the thematic core of the game is something dozens of cultures with divergent mythologies and real world histories have preserved independently of each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're mistaking the set dressing for the thematic core of the game, </div> </div> </div>No. I'm saying I don't think the set dressing works well for the thematic core of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Diluting the origin of the demons involved serves no purpose, and having literally <i>all</i> that has gone wrong for them and for mankind stem from a single unprecedented act of Choice ties thematically to the central question of the gameline in a way six different origin myths can't. </div> </div> </div>Actually it serves a purpose: making the game more fun for more people. That's important, because this is a game. not a philosophy/theology paper. Adding broadness to the game without sacrificing thematic value adds to appeal, replay value, and similar experiential matters. And it can be done without invaliding what people already like about the game; no matter how much they might want to complain otherwise.<br /> <br /> A &quot;single unprecedented act of choice,&quot; does not require a single narrative. In reality the choice that DtF relies on is based on a number of previously existing stories of similar choices.<br /> <br /> DtF, in my opinion as a minimum, is flawed for holding too strongly to one narrative (esp. one so derived from a large number of them) instead of exploring how the central themes you've already cited are central themes to explore because they're wide spread themes that work in multiple (if not almost all) cultural contexts. Unfortunately it also seems to be spilling over from the game into discussions, since you're argument could easily be seen as trying to claim that non-Christian and non-original sin cultures don't have valid claims to have moral stories based on the central themes in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for a 20th Anniversary, I don't recall arguing for one at any point. Can you show me where I have? </div> </div> </div>Maybe, instead of insisting I'm &quot;wrong&quot; about things, you should have actually read what I was saying, and what it was in response to?<br /> <br /> This whole tangent is in response to what I said I would want to see in D20 if it was to be made. That's always been part of the context whether you stated something in support of or against D20 or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T10:27:28-07:00","id":921015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921006#post921006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This statement doesn't seem supported by either the text, or your following comments. What you cite as the thematic core of the game is something dozens of cultures with divergent mythologies and real world histories have preserved independently of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even going to engage with the rest. Are you seriously trying to say that Demon doesn't have, at its core, the theme of free will and its consequences, or the themes of hope/cynicism?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:12:34-07:00","id":921114,"title":"","content":"No, I'm not saying that, and I have no idea how the hell you go that from my statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T15:56:55-07:00","id":921208,"title":"","content":"I never liked Demon, and I always excise it from my game's continuity and canon. I never liked the setup to it, the feel that it was presented as the One True Origin Story for all the other gamelines, or the fact that it treated all non-Judeo-Christian religions as evil creations of the Earthbound. But I could see why other people could like it, it being essentially &quot;Paradise Lost: The RPG&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T17:28:55-07:00","id":921244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=920878#post920878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... yeah, you don't care at all what I'm actually saying about this. Gotcha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Give examples then. Since I seem to be completely missing your point. I mean it kind of sounds like you want New Demon in CWod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T18:35:43-07:00","id":921274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921208#post921208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked Demon, and I always excise it from my game's continuity and canon. I never liked the setup to it, the feel that it was presented as the One True Origin Story for all the other gamelines, or the fact that it treated all non-Judeo-Christian religions as evil creations of the Earthbound. But I could see why other people could like it, it being essentially &quot;Paradise Lost: The RPG&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd better also disavow Vampire for making the Abrahamic God and Flood myth canon as well, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-25-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T19:28:12-07:00","id":921297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921114#post921114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not saying that, and I have no idea how the hell you go that from my statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's fairly straight forward. Let me quote you again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921006#post921006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This statement doesn't seem supported by either the text, or your following comments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'm just a country boy, but where I'm from 'the text' in a debate about a work of literature/art/RPG is that literature. You explicitly state, right here, that my read of the game's core themes is unsupported by the text.<br /> <br /> But, if you're conceding that those are core themes, why don't I move to the rest of that post now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. I'm saying I don't think the set dressing works well for the thematic core of the game. </div> </div> </div>Why, precisely, does the Abrahamic (with Miltonian and Romanticist influence) set dressing not work well for a game that at its core is about the ramifications of free will and the consequences for action, about the battles between hope and cynicism and between faith and despair?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually it serves a purpose: making the game more fun for more people. That's important, because this is a game. not a philosophy/theology paper. Adding broadness to the game without sacrificing thematic value adds to appeal, replay value, and similar experiential matters. And it can be done without invaliding what people already like about the game; no matter how much they might want to complain otherwise. </div> </div> </div>I just don't see why, if you want a game that lets you play demons from multiple mythic models, you don't go play one that already exists? As far as the implication that if I oppose the integration I oppose fun, that isn't true - I just think the game is plenty fun as it is, and stands to gain nothing from incorporating multiple conflicting origin myths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A &quot;single unprecedented act of choice,&quot; does not require a single narrative. In reality the choice that DtF relies on is based on a number of previously existing stories of similar choices. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and every story written has already been written, etc. That doesn't mean that focusing on a specific, archetypal event as the backstory for a game is a bad decision. You may not like it, but that doesn't make it bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DtF, in my opinion as a minimum, is flawed for holding too strongly to one narrative (esp. one so derived from a large number of them) instead of exploring how the central themes you've already cited are central themes to explore because they're wide spread themes that work in multiple (if not almost all) cultural contexts. </div> </div> </div>And that's your opinion, and I respect that but disagree. I think that using a story that the majority of the world's population are exposed to as a mythic background is a fine option for the themes and values of Demon. While broader cultural contexts are good, they are not in fact necessary in each and every work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately it also seems to be spilling over from the game into discussions, since you're argument could easily be seen as trying to claim that non-Christian and non-original sin cultures don't have valid claims to have moral stories based on the central themes in question. </div> </div> </div>And here's where I stop respecting your opinion as your opinion. It's bad form to play the 'you're a crypto-bigot' card without evidence. For the record, I adhere to a non-Abrahamic religious path in my life. My arguments relate solely to what I see as an internally consistent gameline that doesn't need a broader origin, not to, as you're trying to paint it, some real-world agenda against other religions.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think you should apologize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, instead of insisting I'm &quot;wrong&quot; about things, you should have actually read what I was saying, and what it was in response to? </div> </div> </div>I offered a thought unconnected to your debate about D20, not in direct response to it. Maybe, instead of insisting I'm trying to deny that non-Abrahamic religions can be valid, you should actually read what I've been saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T21:24:34-07:00","id":921339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921208#post921208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked Demon, and I always excise it from my game's continuity and canon. I never liked the setup to it, the feel that it was presented as the One True Origin Story for all the other gamelines, or the fact that it treated all non-Judeo-Christian religions as evil creations of the Earthbound. But I could see why other people could like it, it being essentially &quot;Paradise Lost: The RPG&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I find that kind of odd with your Cainites over KOTE types view. I know if I wanted a world of darkness that was less Christian I wouldn't use a game that heavily weighs upon the concept of original Sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T23:37:55-07:00","id":921373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921244#post921244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give examples then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really feel like requoting our entire exchange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean it kind of sounds like you want New Demon in CWod? </div> </div> </div>I said nothing of the sort.<br /> <br /> I sounds far more like you have, &quot;I need to shout down anyone that wants DtD in the WoD for having badwrongfun!&quot; problem, and are letting it color your perception of other people's posts to the point that you're assuming that's what people are trying to say even if they haven't said anything of the sort.<br /> <br /> If you're unsure about something I said, please ask. Demanding I clarify things because you can't be arsed to read what I said isn't going to get us anywhere, because I have no reason to expect you not to twist what I said through whatever filters you're putting up all over again if I just try to reword the same things over and over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921274#post921274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd better also disavow Vampire for making the Abrahamic God and Flood myth canon as well, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite a page where VtM ever actually says that the Noddist mythology of the default VtM game state is actually the objective truth of the game for them to disavow.<br /> <br /> Of course, as has already been covered:<br /> <br /> 1) This is a thread about DtF. People don't need to address VtM in the slightest. If someone has a complaint about something in DtF, it doesn't matter what's in VtM. <br /> <br /> 2) They can not like it about VtM either (though as I noted above, VtM makes it much easier to not hold such things as objective truths anyway), or they can find it less objectionable, or just like how VtM did it better. Coherent stances between the game-lines is not actually necessary to have a valid point about DtF.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921297#post921297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's fairly straight forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's a pretty straight forward example of taking something out of context.<br /> <br /> What you quoted is in response to, &quot;Except it doesn't suggest that at all.&quot; as a response to my statement of, &quot;Again, though, demons not being 100% certain on how the distant past really unfolded, as well as partially losing themselves in the possession process implies that the game's overarching themes are better served with more ambiguity; not less.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not in response to your read of the game's core themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, if you're conceding that those are core themes, why don't I move to the rest of that post now? </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with moving past such things. They're irrelevant to my points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why, precisely, does the Abrahamic (with Miltonian and Romanticist influence) set dressing not work well for a game that at its core is about the ramifications of free will and the consequences for action, about the battles between hope and cynicism and between faith and despair? </div> </div> </div>1) It's not actually Abrahamic. As a practicing member of an Abrahamic faith, DtF stops actually talking to my cultural experiences with it's set dressing almost instantaneously. 99% of it's choices aren't' something that actually follows my religion's mythology. Besides the concept of a supreme creator deity, the importance of names, and angels, nothing about this is actually universal to the Abrahamic faiths.<br /> <br /> 2) The faux-Miltonian derivation of demons actually removes meaningful choice from pretty much every demon besides Lucifer. Having a set history of how things actually happened doesn't help highlight the conflict of choice and consequences, because it means things you had no actual say in. How the Fall and the War happened is set in stone, there are not choices your character can have written into their backstory that are of consequences to game-play. A more ambiguous baseline allows greater ability for the players to explore past choices when making their characters.<br /> <br /> 3) And, of course, it limits choices in the now of the game. All Demon PCs remember the same history of how the world was (just with variable amounts of how much). Having the option for more divergence in how demons remember their ancient history, allows for whole avenues of choice to explore regarding which versions to believe, and whether to seek to reconcile them or find a &quot;canon&quot; to hold on to; with the attended consequences thereof. <br /> <br /> 4) It also harms the efforts to focus on the consequences of free will by making demons (creatures supposedly lacking in true free will) be the source of decision making, while their human hosts (the beings that are supposed to have free will) essentially subsumed and irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just don't see why, if you want a game that lets you play demons from multiple mythic models, you don't go play one that already exists? </div> </div> </div>Who said I don't? If it wasn't clear... DtF is not one of my favorite games (though there aren't that many, &quot;play as a demon&quot; games out there).<br /> <br /> I am capable of liking DtF enough to see that it could be a game I really like, and I'm capable of expressing how to change it to orient it better in that direction. It doesn't really matter if that's not what you want, because I'm not trying to express your opinions for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the implication that if I oppose the integration I oppose fun, that isn't true - I just think the game is plenty fun as it is, and stands to gain nothing from incorporating multiple conflicting origin myths. </div> </div> </div>And yet you basically prove it true. What you aren't really addressing is that the game can be expanded without actually taking away what you find fun about it, while increasing other people's fun with the game. Advocating in the abstract against changing things without sacrificing what's already there is same is arguing against fun; just other people's fun instead of your own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You may not like it, but that doesn't make it bad. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make it <i>good</i> either. Which isn't something you've actually bothered to try to make a case for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that using a story that the majority of the world's population are exposed to as a mythic background is a fine option for the themes and values of Demon. </div> </div> </div>Not that it entirely relevant, but the majority of the world's population aren't exposed to this specific myth in any real detail, and don't hold it as a cultural tradition for those that do. It's a Christian specific take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And here's where I stop respecting your opinion as your opinion. </div> </div> </div>That's... meaningless. What do you treat my opinions as if they aren't my opinions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's bad form to play the 'you're a crypto-bigot' card without evidence. </div> </div> </div>I don't see you actually caring about bad form unless it's aimed at you... so... yeah. When you post with no respect to form, you should expect getting &quot;bad form&quot; in response; not apologies.<br /> <br /> Also. I didn't call you a crypto-bigot. I said your argumentation could be read as implying bigoted biases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I offered a thought unconnected to your debate about D20, not in direct response to it. </div> </div> </div>You can't have both. You directly responded to my posts about my points aboud D20, even if your thoughts were not about D20. Any attempt to take my comments about D20 out of the context of D20 is disingenuous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, instead of insisting I'm trying to deny that non-Abrahamic religions can be valid, you should actually read what I've been saying. </div> </div> </div>I have. Though I'm waiting for anything more than, &quot;I like DtF how it is, so changing can't possibly have merit.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T00:01:45-07:00","id":921384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921373#post921373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, that's a pretty straight forward example of taking something out of context.<br /> <br /> What you quoted is in response to, &quot;Except it doesn't suggest that at all.&quot; as a response to my statement of, &quot;Again, though, demons not being 100% certain on how the distant past really unfolded, as well as partially losing themselves in the possession process implies that the game's overarching themes are better served with more ambiguity; not less.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was not in response to your read of the game's core themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's funny. You then immediately attacked what I claimed as core themes on the same line.<br /> <br /> Also, as I said then, you're mistaking set dressing for themes. The game's core themes have nothing to do with ambiguity about the past.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) It's not actually Abrahamic. As a practicing member of an Abrahamic faith, DtF stops actually talking to my cultural experiences with it's set dressing almost instantaneously. 99% of it's choices aren't' something that actually follows my religion's mythology. Besides the concept of a supreme creator deity, the importance of names, and angels, nothing about this is actually universal to the Abrahamic faiths. </div> </div> </div>The entire narrative is steeped in Judeo-Christianity and its various popular conceptions. That isn't really up for debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) The faux-Miltonian derivation of demons actually removes meaningful choice from pretty much every demon besides Lucifer. Having a set history of how things actually happened doesn't help highlight the conflict of choice and consequences, because it means things you had no actual say in. How the Fall and the War happened is set in stone, there are not choices your character can have written into their backstory that are of consequences to game-play. A more ambiguous baseline allows greater ability for the players to explore past choices when making their characters. </div> </div> </div>Of course, the choices that matter are the choices in the present of the game, not the past, so it actually doesn't remove 'meaningful choice' from every demon. All it does is say 'you fought. You lost. Time to see what you can make of the new world.'<br /> <br /> There is also nothing preventing the players from exploring past choices - vast swathes of history were left deliberately vague to leave exactly how things played out, beyond the broadest strokes, to the ST and the players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) And, of course, it limits choices in the now of the game. All Demon PCs remember the same history of how the world was (just with variable amounts of how much). Having the option for more divergence in how demons remember their ancient history, allows for whole avenues of choice to explore regarding which versions to believe, and whether to seek to reconcile them or find a &quot;canon&quot; to hold on to; with the attended consequences thereof. </div> </div> </div>And that's where different perspectives come into play. Two demons can perceive the exact same event differently, even without the frailties and biases of their new hosts. There is nothing stopping you from doing this in the game as written.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) It also harms the efforts to focus on the consequences of free will by making demons (creatures supposedly lacking in true free will) be the source of decision making, while their human hosts (the beings that are supposed to have free will) essentially subsumed and irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>This is going to be the case unless you radically change how Demon views hosts in the first place, but struggle with them for control and will is a fundamental part of the setting as is anyway. It also doesn't diminish any effort to focus on the consequences of free will - demons are the source of their initial decisions, humans or not, in the source material (except for the perspective that all decisions are preordained, etc, etc)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who said I don't? If it wasn't clear... DtF is not one of my favorite games (though there aren't that many, &quot;play as a demon&quot; games out there).<br /> <br /> I am capable of liking DtF enough to see that it could be a game I really like, and I'm capable of expressing how to change it to orient it better in that direction. It doesn't really matter if that's not what you want, because I'm not trying to express your opinions for you. </div> </div> </div>You can express how to change it, and I can express that I disagree with your proposed changes. That's what discussion is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yet you basically prove it true. What you aren't really addressing is that the game can be expanded without actually taking away what you find fun about it, while increasing other people's fun with the game. Advocating in the abstract against changing things without sacrificing what's already there is same is arguing against fun; just other people's fun instead of your own. </div> </div> </div>My argument is simply that the game is internally consistent, and anything that compromises that needs to be weighed against the overall value gained. I don't think it's outweighed by a few more people enjoying it more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't make it <i>good</i> either. Which isn't something you've actually bothered to try to make a case for. </div> </div> </div>I've never tried to claim it is objectively good, nor am I about to start.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not that it entirely relevant, but the majority of the world's population aren't exposed to this specific myth in any real detail, and don't hold it as a cultural tradition for those that do. It's a Christian specific take. </div> </div> </div>It's a Christian specific, sure, but the Abrahamic religions have enough cross-pollination for it to work with any of them, and the last time I checked they constituted a majority of the global population.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see you actually caring about bad form unless it's aimed at you... so... yeah. When you post with no respect to form, you should expect getting &quot;bad form&quot; in response; not apologies.<br /> <br /> Also. I didn't call you a crypto-bigot. I said your argumentation could be read as implying bigoted biases. </div> </div> </div>Tomato, tomato. As far as not caring about bad form, I'm pretty sure this is the first instance of serious bad form in our exchange, or would you like to point to an earlier one?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't have both. You directly responded to my posts about my points aboud D20, even if your thoughts were not about D20. Any attempt to take my comments about D20 out of the context of D20 is disingenuous. </div> </div> </div>I made a post about how I view Demon. You responded. Only after you responded did I respond to you. Prior to you engaging me, I not once made any posts talking to or about you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have. Though I'm waiting for anything more than, &quot;I like DtF how it is, so changing can't possibly have merit.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And I'm waiting for anything more than 'I don't like DtF how it is, so we should change it' - and an apology for your attempt to paint me with the bigot brush.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T01:56:06-07:00","id":921407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921384#post921384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's funny. You then immediately attacked what I claimed as core themes on the same line.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I didn't. &quot;I'm going to outright lie about what you said, but you owe me an apology,&quot; is a great example of bad form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire narrative is steeped in Judeo-Christianity and its various popular conceptions. That isn't really up for debate. </div> </div> </div>Oh I can debate one aspect of this plenty actually.<br /> <br /> There's nothing &quot;Judeo&quot; about it. Period and full stop. Jewish orthodoxy regarding demons treats the whole Essene/proto-Christian lore of the fallen angel as heresy. There's no specific Jewish demonology before later Kabbalistic response to Christian demonology; the origin of evil spirits was a matter of a mess of either contradictory or at least inconsistent folklore (mostly seeming to be shared with a number of contemporary folklores and mythologies from the ancient Middle East)<br /> <br /> And now I get much more serious about the bigotry thing:<br /> <br /> When you move from Abrahamic, to Judeo-Christian, when you really mean Christian? It's a pattern/tactic that has a huge amount of history in antisemetic literature to erase the validity of Judaism as anything but an outdated precursor to Christianity. So if you wanted me to even back off this, let alone apologize? Right here was a move in the exact wrong direction. I try not to get too up-in-arms about this because most people don't realize this, and the phrase &quot;Judeo-Christian,&quot; sounds academic/neutral that they don't think about the implications. But yeah... not a good way to say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, the choices that matter are the choices in the present of the game, not the past, so it actually doesn't remove 'meaningful choice' from every demon. All it does is say 'you fought. You lost. Time to see what you can make of the new world.' </div> </div> </div>The choices of the past matter to the present of the game. So none of the counter-argument holds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's where different perspectives come into play. Two demons can perceive the exact same event differently, even without the frailties and biases of their new hosts. There is nothing stopping you from doing this in the game as written. </div> </div> </div>Perspectives aren't really varied enough to actually do this with the game as written. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is going to be the case unless you radically change how Demon views hosts in the first place, but struggle with them for control and will is a fundamental part of the setting as is anyway. It also doesn't diminish any effort to focus on the consequences of free will - demons are the source of their initial decisions, humans or not, in the source material (except for the perspective that all decisions are preordained, etc, etc) </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, it is a problem beyond the scope of just the set-dressing, but the set-dressing doesn't help here; it hurts. The set dressing is one where humans have &quot;true&quot; free will, and demons don't, but then the game sets up demons as the source of dramatic conflict to explore the consequences of free will and choice. <br /> <br /> You also seem to be waffling between Free Will, and Compatibalism. Free Will doesn't just work for initial decisions, as a philosophic construct it should be constant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can express how to change it, and I can express that I disagree with your proposed changes. That's what discussion is. </div> </div> </div>Well, a discussion is when we go beyond simply expressing our opinions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My argument is simply that the game is internally consistent, and anything that compromises that needs to be weighed against the overall value gained. I don't think it's outweighed by a few more people enjoying it more. </div> </div> </div>This argument fails because it assumes change inherently means compromising internal consistency. You can change it to something broader and still internally consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never tried to claim it is objectively good, nor am I about to start. </div> </div> </div>Then why should your desire to argue the contrary position as bad be taken seriously?<br /> <br /> If you're not willing to actually support the current state of the game as good (noting that you added the word objective, not me), then you don't really have any solid basis for saying that anything is actually being compromised for the value that could be gained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a Christian specific, sure, but the Abrahamic religions have enough cross-pollination for it to work with any of them, and the last time I checked they constituted a majority of the global population. </div> </div> </div>And there we go with the lumping of wildly different beliefs together as one group.<br /> <br /> You realize Judaism and Islam both reject the concept of demons coming from the fall of angels? DtF doesn't work with either religion. The closest it gets are a schismatic group of Jews from 2000 years ago that don't exist anymore (outside of those that joined Christianity), and some cross pollination between Kabbalistic demonology (which isn't representative of the majority beliefs for Christianity or Judaism).<br /> <br /> The silly part of all of this is that either the Jewish or Muslim take on demons would have actually made for a game that functions within the wider WoD much more easily than the way DtF went. If DtF was actually compatible with Abrahamic mythologies in general, rather than one specific Christian version, a lot of the complaints about the game wouldn't be nearly as strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as not caring about bad form, I'm pretty sure this is the first instance of serious bad form in our exchange, or would you like to point to an earlier one? </div> </div> </div>There's a serious amount of context removal in your posts as noted already.<br /> <br /> Also, you might notice I didn't just say, &quot;you're guilty of bad form too.&quot;<br /> <br /> I tend not to take much stock in the umbrage of people that complain about bad form only when it pertains to them and don't call it out in general. I don't expect people to play mod, but if you only call things out because they're aimed at you, how does anyone know the difference between self-serving rhetoric or actual bad feelings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I made a post about how I view Demon. You responded. Only after you responded did I respond to you. Prior to you engaging me, I not once made any posts talking to or about you. </div> </div> </div>So... pot calling the kettle black then? You get to come at me with &quot;tomato tomato,&quot; but here you are doing exactly that. Your post didn't quote me, but it only makes sense in the context of what I'd said in the posts before it as a response to those posts. But that's a kind of technicality that's fine when it works for you then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm waiting for anything more than 'I don't like DtF how it is, so we should change it' - and an apology for your attempt to paint me with the bigot brush. </div> </div> </div>This is a complaints about DtF thread. The whole point is to voice complaints about it. If you want more than that, you should either start a different thread, or at least actually try to encourage discussion about going deeper into those complaints instead of just trying to dismiss them.<br /> <br /> And I'll consider the apology, but it's really hard to convince someone that you've had a good shower after getting off a high stinky horse over the Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T04:53:59-07:00","id":921432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921407#post921407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I didn't. &quot;I'm going to outright lie about what you said, but you owe me an apology,&quot; is a great example of bad form.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921006#post921006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This statement doesn't seem supported by either the text, or your following comments. What you cite as the thematic core of the game is something dozens of cultures with divergent mythologies and real world histories have preserved independently of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but that sure looks like the same line to me, and it sure looks like you're engaging with the claim of core themes.<br /> <br /> Until such a time as you apologize for trying for the bigotry brush, I have no further comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T05:43:10-07:00","id":921449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921274#post921274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd better also disavow Vampire for making the Abrahamic God and Flood myth canon as well, then.</div> </div> </div> </div> Revised Vampire maybe, since that edition treated the Caine story as hard fact. 1e and 2e treated the Caine myth as a theory rather than a hard fact. Granted it was the most popular theory among elder Kindred in those editions, but unlike Revised, Caine was about as relevant to your average Neonate or Ancilla in 1e and 2e as Osiris is relevant to your modern-day American.<br /> <br /> And I already disavow Revised Edition in its entirety anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:39:19-07:00","id":921593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921449#post921449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised Vampire maybe, since that edition treated the Caine story as hard fact. 1e and 2e treated the Caine myth as a theory rather than a hard fact. Granted it was the most popular theory among elder Kindred in those editions, but unlike Revised, Caine was about as relevant to your average Neonate or Ancilla in 1e and 2e as Osiris is relevant to your modern-day American.<br /> <br /> And I already disavow Revised Edition in its entirety anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a modern-day Anerican who sometimes prays to Osiris, I'm not sure I grasp your metaphor <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:40:47-07:00","id":921594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921449#post921449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised Vampire maybe, since that edition treated the Caine story as hard fact. 1e and 2e treated the Caine myth as a theory rather than a hard fact. Granted it was the most popular theory among elder Kindred in those editions, but unlike Revised, Caine was about as relevant to your average Neonate or Ancilla in 1e and 2e as Osiris is relevant to your modern-day American.<br /> <br /> And I already disavow Revised Edition in its entirety anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1e Had caine hanging out in a bar in Berlin. This is before the whole conceit of the Embrace is built upon the idea that it comes from his sin. That you are damned not by your actions, but by the &quot;Original Sin&quot; of Caine.<br /> <br /> At least KOTE can blame themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T11:53:26-07:00","id":921598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=921432#post921432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about you, but that sure looks like the same line to me, and it sure looks like you're engaging with the claim of core themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Engaging&quot; well there's a goal post shift from &quot;attacking.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, I engaging with them, but not on the grounds of attacking or contesting them. I engaged with them to point out that they aren't unique or uniquely well served by the set dressing of DtF; regardless of how internally consistent it might be. I never once attacked or even questioned your phrasing of the core themes of the game - because as I've noted the specifics aren't really that important to my point - and yet you directly said I have. And not in a round-about-lets-pick-at-inferences sort of way that could have been &quot;engaged&quot; but was misinterpreted as &quot;attacked.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until such a time as you apologize for trying for the bigotry brush, I have no further comment. </div> </div> </div>Have fun with that. I've seen very few people actually hold to such tactics. Engaging in discussion after stating that you'd like something, including a &quot;I'm going to get a last point it before I'm going to not say more&quot; tends to blunt any claim at true hurt feelings to inspire any contrition on my part.<br /> <br /> And you're not getting an apology. I'm perfectly willing to give you the benefit of the doubt that this isn't malicious in intent, but that doesn't put the onus on me to apologize for your wording after you decided to double down from &quot;dude that could be taken as kinda bigoted,&quot; to, &quot;dude, that's actually bigoted.&quot;.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> As a side note to all this, over 80% of Muslims live in either Muslim majority or non-Christian majority countries. Only 3% of Muslims live in Europe and the Americas. So while Abrahamic religions just squeeze out a majority of global populations (~53%) that relies heavily on over a billion (a lot more than 3% of the global population) people that don't have any significant ties to Christian culture and mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T19:51:24-07:00","id":921823,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Knock off the arguing, now. Heavy Arms you can stay out of this discussion now too, since you accused someone of being a bigot for using a commonly accepted term in a non academically precise manner. That's a personal attack, I'm being generous by only issuing a thread ban.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T17:17:11-07:00","id":922304,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong part of the reason I liked Demon: The Fallen was it's epic finger to Werewolf's having told &quot;The Truth of the CosmosTM&quot; first?<br /> <br /> I will, however make some points.<br /> <br /> 1. <b><i>Demon: The Fallen </i>isn't based on Milton. It's based on <i>Memnoch the Devil</i>: </b>The demons in D:TF are basically the tortured Byronic Ricean hero of that novel (and I don't mean Lestat) which is why the game feels so much like Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> It *IS* Anne Rice.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Demons still existed alongside humanity: </b>Demons were summoned constantly by magicians from Hell, only to be returned or to become part of the 666 Earthbound.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>It pretty effectively repudiates Christianity: </b>Jesus can't be true in a world abandoned by God and angels. There's the hint Jesus and Muhammed were inspired by an exiled Gabriel but the game never got into that and it's still making it clearly not God.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>90% of all Demons were Evil: </b>This is actually a complaint I had about the game that it was a game built around the redemption of Fallen Angels and it seemed most of them weren't.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Demon powers suck:</b> You could maybe someday destroy California but it was useless on a more day-to-day level.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>As a crossover fiction, it sucks with Werewolf and Mage but worked well with Vampire: </b>Would I have appreciated more alternate takes like, &quot;Demons are just Incarnae and Spirits who have taken on the Christian mythology of their hosts?&quot; Possibly.<br /> <br /> But yes, I really do like sticking the finger to the Werewolf take on the subject matter.<br /> <br /> 7. <b>The fiction was actually pretty good: </b>Really, I recommend people read the anthology.<br /> <br /> I do think any D20 game would be better as demons always having been around, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-27-2016, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:11:42-07:00","id":922772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=922304#post922304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong part of the reason I liked Demon: The Fallen was it's epic finger to Werewolf's having told &quot;The Truth of the CosmosTM&quot; first?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually Mage. It's basically the polar opposite in using many of the same settings but having completely inverted assumptions and weighted importance. Also, Werewolf already gave everything Demon assumed the finger when it was created as a very different thing from Vampire, since Demon just goes full tilt with the Noddist part of Vampire. So, really, D:tF didn't really do anything that hadn't been done before in any interesting, new ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:55:37-07:00","id":922798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=922772#post922772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was actually Mage. It's basically the polar opposite in using many of the same settings but having completely inverted assumptions and weighted importance. Also, Werewolf already gave everything Demon assumed the finger when it was created as a very different thing from Vampire, since Demon just goes full tilt with the Noddist part of Vampire. So, really, D:tF didn't really do anything that hadn't been done before in any interesting, new ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I disagree strongly since it was the first personal horror game since Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:27:19-07:00","id":922936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=922798#post922798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, I disagree strongly since it was the first personal horror game since Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Wraith is only partially about personal horror. It's also about the hope of getting out of a miserable situation and stopping the voice of doubt in your head that sabotages everything productive, or at least non self-destructive, that you try to do.<br /> <br /> Secondly, my post was regarding your reading of Demon as &quot;telling off&quot; Werewolf. To reiterate the point, given that Demon was basically acting as a metaplot add-on to Vampire in terms of setting, as Vampire became more and more hardline Noddist out of character, it came pre-told off by all the games between Vampires and Demon. To place stock in Demon as an &quot;answer&quot; to Werewolf is to confuse who came first and who's &quot;rebelling&quot; against an &quot;establishment&quot;, because at last I checked, Vampire has higher sales and tends to distort things its way in a manner that's not good for other games when it comes to the metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T18:17:09-07:00","id":922961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=922936#post922936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, Wraith is only partially about personal horror. It's also about the hope of getting out of a miserable situation and stopping the voice of doubt in your head that sabotages everything productive, or at least non self-destructive, that you try to do.<br /> <br /> Secondly, my post was regarding your reading of Demon as &quot;telling off&quot; Werewolf. To reiterate the point, given that Demon was basically acting as a metaplot add-on to Vampire in terms of setting, as Vampire became more and more hardline Noddist out of character, it came pre-told off by all the games between Vampires and Demon. To place stock in Demon as an &quot;answer&quot; to Werewolf is to confuse who came first and who's &quot;rebelling&quot; against an &quot;establishment&quot;, because at last I checked, Vampire has higher sales and tends to distort things its way in a manner that's not good for other games when it comes to the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying I like D:TF because it has a nice contradiction of Werewolf cosmology where you have two authoratative sources with definitive answers which are contradictory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T21:42:05-07:00","id":923058,"title":"","content":"I never got any sort of personal horror vibe off of Demon. The gist of every game I ever came across or heard about always seemed to be &quot;Regain your awesome Demon powers. Give God the finger. Profit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon added to the metaplot of Vampire the same way Phantom Menace added to the metaplot of Star Wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:05:58-07:00","id":923072,"title":"","content":"I don't know that I agree, CP. Any oWoD game can be run as a power-focused B-grade movie, but that doesn't mean it's true of the games in and of themselves. I've always gotten a very strong horror vibe, both personal and to a degree existential, from Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T22:33:37-07:00","id":923084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923058#post923058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got any sort of personal horror vibe off of Demon. The gist of every game I ever came across or heard about always seemed to be &quot;Regain your awesome Demon powers. Give God the finger. Profit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, I never actually encountered anyone who ran Demon that way before. For me it was all about the horror of being in a world which you couldn't help and which was ruined because you had disrupted the universe to the point it was unsalvagable.<br /> <br /> I ran a lot of games about demons basically taking the role of Guardian Angels because with God absent, they were the closet thing to a benveolent God left.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:24:31-07:00","id":923233,"title":"","content":"we never found that as well CP. For us it was always the 'become the human' part, and we always focused on it. We didn't get 'whatever-powered teen superhero wannabe&quot;, at least not more than some players do for every line... Sorry that was your experience...<br /> <br /> As for criticism we didn't like the THIS IS THE TRUTH aspects, but that was a problem of the whole Cwod, and while we did like the pseudo-abrahamic trappings, we ditched eden, adam, eve, lucifer, etc, and went with a more gnostic trapping: demiurge becomes self-aware, creates archons to help hold human minds back, Him is an assholhe because of that.<br /> <br /> However that's the point of view of rebelious archons so it's probably biased. Was the demiurge an asshole trying to hiold the enightened humanity and the fallen were anarchistic heroes, or was he acting with utmost love because the gnostic truth is bullshit and it's a cold, dark universe out there full of cthulian things, and the fallen were just rebelious pricks? Those two things fixed most lore problems for us, since we never did crossover anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T07:25:51-07:00","id":923234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923084#post923084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weird, I never actually encountered anyone who ran Demon that way before. For me it was all about the horror of being in a world which you couldn't help and which was ruined because you had disrupted the universe to the point it was unsalvagable.<br /> <br /> I ran a lot of games about demons basically taking the role of Guardian Angels because with God absent, they were the closet thing to a benveolent God left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you see personal horror there? It's a fatalist view of the world where you can change little or nothing, but you yourself are not the biggest threat to your own well being and you do not need to fight your own personal demons on a daily basis to keep ticking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:09:36-07:00","id":923260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DiBastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923233#post923233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we never found that as well CP. For us it was always the 'become the human' part, and we always focused on it. We didn't get 'whatever-powered teen superhero wannabe&quot;, at least not more than some players do for every line... Sorry that was your experience...<br /> <br /> As for criticism we didn't like the THIS IS THE TRUTH aspects, but that was a problem of the whole Cwod, and while we did like the pseudo-abrahamic trappings, we ditched eden, adam, eve, lucifer, etc, and went with a more gnostic trapping: demiurge becomes self-aware, creates archons to help hold human minds back, Him is an assholhe because of that.<br /> <br /> However that's the point of view of rebelious archons so it's probably biased. Was the demiurge an asshole trying to hiold the enightened humanity and the fallen were anarchistic heroes, or was he acting with utmost love because the gnostic truth is bullshit and it's a cold, dark universe out there full of cthulian things, and the fallen were just rebelious pricks? Those two things fixed most lore problems for us, since we never did crossover anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the Demon: The Fallen novels gave an alternate, &quot;You know God well could have left because he was trying to save the world, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which kind of shocked and horrified the Demon who listened to the possibility.<br /> <br /> My personal favorite take on the subject is the Demons rebelled but eventually became so corrupted and twisted that the war was actually Black and Black Morality.<br /> <br /> The other Angels (The Loyalists) all becoming evil psycho fundamentalists.<br /> <br /> And THAT'S when God left....by merging with humanity and giving them True MagickTM.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:15:30-07:00","id":923265,"title":"","content":"See I was never really wowed by the novels either. I worked at a used book store that had books two and three of that trilogy sitting on the shelf gathering dust for years. I read them both gradually while I was there and just never felt especially grabbed or interested by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:38:24-07:00","id":923277,"title":"","content":"In fairness, and with the disclaimer I wasn't particularly impressed either, trilogies work better if you start with the first one. It's often where the emotional ties are forged to the major characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T08:39:36-07:00","id":923278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923234#post923234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where do you see personal horror there? It's a fatalist view of the world where you can change little or nothing, but you yourself are not the biggest threat to your own well being and you do not need to fight your own personal demons on a daily basis to keep ticking.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, Demons were basically suffering the world's worst case of PTSD thanks to Hell.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it wasn't real PTSD but Hollywood PTSD that came with a dose of psychotic desire to lash out.<br /> <br /> Every demon could be good and wants to be good on some level but they also want to HURT other people.<br /> <br /> To destroy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T10:08:55-07:00","id":923332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923277#post923277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness, and with the disclaimer I wasn't particularly impressed either, trilogies work better if you start with the first one. It's often where the emotional ties are forged to the major characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and that thought had occurred to me as well. I've started other series in the middle before though and been sufficiently drawn in that it didn't matter I was lacking context. It wasn't that events didn't make sense, I just didn't care about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T04:45:36-07:00","id":926991,"title":"","content":"My primary gripe is that one of the primary objectives in Demon, the finding and seducing of Thralls, is essentially a solo endeavour. Sure, the system just fine but when one player is doing this the other players can do nothing but sit there and watch, which really slows down the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T16:37:30-07:00","id":927333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/106123-what-are-the-main-critisisms-of-demon-the-fallen?p=923058#post923058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got any sort of personal horror vibe off of Demon. The gist of every game I ever came across or heard about always seemed to be &quot;Regain your awesome Demon powers. Give God the finger. Profit.&quot;<br /> <br /> Demon added to the metaplot of Vampire the same way Phantom Menace added to the metaplot of Star Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hoenstly. the problem it is that the book doesnt really states how the Personal Horror works (mainly through the artwork). the way i Dm it is making the players not being aware that they are demons and slowly starting to remember things...and also using their apocaliptic forms with out realizing what they are doing (among other things) also, theres the fact that i allow my players to create their demons...But i dont allow them to create the &quot;Human Host.&quot; i randomly offer them to my players","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}